cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use OpenInterBias, please cite it as below, and also cite OpenBias, on which it builds."
title: "OpenInterBias: open-set discovery of intersectional bias in text-to-image models"
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
authors:
  - given-names: Andrea
    family-names: Giampietro
  - given-names: Irene
    family-names: Verria
repository-code: "https://github.com/giampyhatesyou/OpenInterBias"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A post-hoc extension of OpenBias from single-attribute to intersectional (joint-attribute)
  bias detection in text-to-image models. It scans every same-subject attribute pair proposed
  by the LLM, measures dependence with bias-corrected normalized mutual information, tests it
  with permutation tests under Benjamini-Hochberg FDR control, and filters out prompts that
  already state one of the attributes.
keywords:
  - text-to-image
  - bias detection
  - intersectionality
  - fairness
  - mutual information
  - multiple testing
references:
